  "limits": [
    "Dance starts low and cycles high then middle after full-target tile completion. Overflow does not advance the phase.",
    "The fixed midpoint is the floor midpoint of the initial missing-interval hull, not uncovered rank. Split once there; no tile or work unit crosses it.",
    "The middle front advances upward and falls back to low when no upper-half work remains. Planner entries are bounded by original gaps plus four.",
    "At most three adaptive work units interleave, timed by their own execution excluding pauses and other units.",
    "Restart recalculates the pivot and resets low on saved complement. Exact scalar union is preserved; submission sequence may differ.",
    "Job/configuration/table identity, schema 7, protocol, receipts and capabilities are unchanged. Scalar --order and block claims remain separate.",
    "Both kernels tested on HIP/CUDA; group-8 spots cover eight ordinals. No exhaustive kernel-by-device product, fleet scaling or new partition claim.",
    "Seven focused host sanitizer gates; no claim of whole-application or device-code sanitizer coverage.",
    "No new device arithmetic or throughput claim. Legacy random dance is not reproduced. Additional random traversal semantics and alternative minikey orders remain pending.",
    "Public fixtures only; no enrollment credentials or journal databases archived."
  ],
